behaviors during deployment. This
combinatorial

41
00:02:44,569 --> 00:02:49,090
explosion makes comprehensive testing
exponentially more difficult but essential

42
00:02:49,090 --> 00:02:53,030
for meaningful safety claims. A model
passing most safety

43
00:02:53,030 --> 00:02:57,349
benchmarks might still harbor dangerous
capability combinations that weren't

44
00:02:57,349 --> 00:03:00,469
explicitly tested. This is why we need to
move

45
00:03:00,469 --> 00:03:04,030
measurement of safety critical properties
of a system towards

46
00:03:04,030 --> 00:03:09,509
comprehensive evaluations. Effective
safety assessment requires measuring three
distinct

47
00:03:10,550 --> 00:03:17,310
capabilities, propensities and control
dangerous capabilities. Evaluations
establish upper

48
00:03:17,310 --> 00:03:19,750
bounds on what models can do when pushed
to

49
00:03:19,750 --> 00:03:22,939
their limits through techniques like
scaffolding and tool augmentation.

50
00:03:24,129 --> 00:03:28,050
Propensity evaluations reveal what
behaviors models tend to exhibit

51
00:03:28,050 --> 00:03:32,530
by default, measuring behavioral
tendencies rather than just maximum

52
00:03:32,530 --> 00:03:37,409
abilities. Control evaluations verify
whether safety protocols remain effective

53
00:03:37,409 --> 00:03:40,930
when models actively try to circumvent
them. This three

54
00:03:40,930 --> 00:03:44,689
part taxonomy provides a systematic
framework for safety measurement

55
00:03:44,770 --> 00:03:47,610
that helps answer the most decision
relevant questions about

56
00:03:47,610 --> 00:03:52,539
